Narrows I7's revert exemption in sim.rs `record` back to the author's own
re-issue, as before the I7 half of 15d13ea: a write that reaches a vector its
author's revert discarded is exempt only if the node making it wrote both
records. The fix exempts any write that reaches such a vector, a merge that
includes the re-issued counter too, since nobody else ever held the discarded
record (DESIGN.md §14.1 I7, §8.3). The replacement of the discarded record
(8d4620d) is left alone.

